00:00:00,820 --> 00:00:02,020
In the next few minutes,

2
00:00:02,040 --> 00:00:03,330
you will be able to.

3
00:00:04,170 --> 00:00:06,490
Its core job is easy to state.

4
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:07,820
Given some text,

5
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:09,069
predict the text that is

6
00:00:09,068 --> 00:00:10,690
most likely to come next.

7
00:00:11,495 --> 00:00:13,465
Paris gets a very high one.

8
00:00:13,485 --> 00:00:15,475
Most other words get almost none.

9
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:18,267
It picks one, adds it to the text,

10
00:00:18,287 --> 00:00:19,280
and repeats.

11
00:00:19,410 --> 00:00:20,690
One word at a time,

12
00:00:20,710 --> 00:00:23,010
that is how a full answer gets written.

13
00:00:23,865 --> 00:00:25,788
More precisely, it works in

14
00:00:25,787 --> 00:00:27,675
small pieces called tokens,

15
00:00:27,695 --> 00:00:28,978
which are often parts of

16
00:00:28,977 --> 00:00:30,745
words rather than whole words.
